  "id": "COMPOUND:28424 - PROTEIN:1503",
  "verbalization": "Kuanoniamine D appears to exert its biological effects through a series of target-mediated pathways that ultimately lead to the inhibition of G1/S-specific cyclin-D1. The evidence suggests that Kuanoniamine D acts as a target of multiple compounds, which in turn target cyclin-D1. Specifically, Kuanoniamine D directly interacts with Cytochrome c4, which is then targeted by 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin and 6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin. These secondary targets all ultimately lead to the suppression of G1/S-specific cyclin-D1. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between Kuanoniamine D and cyclin-D1, though the exact nature of the interaction between Kuanoniamine D and Cytochrome c4 remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a consistent and plausible pathway, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction and the precise mechanism of action.",
